<title>USA: Haddon Heights, N.J., may seek bond recount--paper.</title>
<headline>Haddon Heights, N.J., may seek bond recount--paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Haddon Heights, N.J., School Superintendent Edward Snyder said he would seek a recount of a bond referendum Saturday that was defeated by four votes, Philadelphia Inquirer reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>Voters approved by 718 to 658 one question authorizing $2.3 million for new technology and repairs. But they voted down a second $1.5 million question on whether to finance improvements needed to make two schools handicapped-accessible.</p>
<p>The vote was 687 in favor and 691 against.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
